# OpenGunstore production env (frappe_docker). Copy to deploy/prod/.env on the
# server and fill in. The real .env holds secrets and MUST NOT be committed
# (it is gitignored).
#
# The host's reverse proxy (Caddy) owns 80/443 and fronts us, so we use the
# noproxy override (no Traefik). TLS + routing live in the proxy
# (see deploy/prod/Caddyfile.example), NOT here.

# --- Image: built by .github/workflows/release-image.yml (or by you from deploy/prod/Dockerfile), pushed to a registry ---
# The stack runs linux/amd64 only (the compose files pin it). Build your own with
#   docker build --platform linux/amd64 -f deploy/prod/Dockerfile -t <image>:<tag> .
CUSTOM_IMAGE=<registry>/<image>
# A product release tag (vX.Y.Z: the release job adds it to the image main pushed) for the first start;
# every deploy then rewrites this line to the tag it rolled out (auto_deploy.sh).
CUSTOM_TAG=vX.Y.Z
# always: pull the image from the registry on every `up` (the default for a published image).
# never:  use the image already on this machine and never contact a registry. Set this for an image you built
#         locally, and skip `up.sh pull`; with `always` Docker looks for your local-only image in a registry and fails.
PULL_POLICY=always
# Fallback tag only; CUSTOM_TAG above takes precedence. Keep aligned with docs/versions.md.
ERPNEXT_VERSION=v16.51.1

# --- Database: self-hosted MariaDB container (compose.mariadb.yaml) ---
# Also used as the --mariadb-root-password during site bootstrap.
DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_strong_db_root_password

# --- Site ---
# The Frappe site name MUST equal the public host that Caddy proxies here.
FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER=pos.example.com

# --- Web port (compose.noproxy.yaml): frontend bound to localhost; Caddy proxies to it ---
HTTP_PUBLISH_PORT=127.0.0.1:8080

# --- Local distributor catalog (optional) ---
# Only for a store whose Data Service Settings › Catalog source is Local: starts
# the queue-catalog worker (deploy/prod/compose.extensions.yaml). A store on the
# Data Service leaves this unset and never runs that container.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=catalog

# --- Remote MCP connector (optional; see docs/self-hosting.md#remote-mcp-connector-optional) ---
# 0 = auto_deploy.sh skips the MCP step entirely and never pulls an MCP image. Leave it 0 unless you
# publish your own MCP server image: the image the default points at is private and cannot be pulled
# without access, so a fresh install that left this unset would try to pull it on every deploy.
MCP_ENABLED=0
# To run the connector, remove the line above (or set 1) and set the image you publish:
# MCP_IMAGE=<registry>/<image>
# MCP_TAG=sha-<7>   Run this image tag instead of the one pinned in deploy/prod/mcp/version.env.

# --- Backups: ofelia cron runs `bench --site all backup` (compose.backup-cron.yaml) ---
BACKUP_CRONSTRING=@every 6h

# --- Optional nginx tuning (sane defaults already applied) ---
# CLIENT_MAX_BODY_SIZE=50m
# PROXY_READ_TIMEOUT=120
